## 1. Getting started

Focus CRM keeps everything about your customers in one place:

- **Contacts**: the people you talk to
- **Companies**: the organisations they work for
- **Deals**: the sales opportunities you are working on
- **Activities and tasks**: the work around them (calls, emails, meetings, notes, follow-ups)
- **Tickets**: customer support requests

Every record is linked, so opening any one of them shows you the full story.

### Open the app

An administrator starts it once from the project folder:

    npm install
    npm run dev

Then open http://localhost:3000 in your browser.

### Sign in

The sign-in page lists the users found in your data. Click a name to fill in the email, or type it.

- Email (example): `mmitchell@hubspot.com` (Morgan Mitchell, workspace admin, pre-filled)
- Password: `demo123`

> **Tip:** The very first time the app opens, it reads the CSV files in the `Data` folder and builds
> the CRM from them. You'll see "Importing records from the CSV files…" for a moment. After that,
> it opens straight away.

