## 4. End-to-end walkthrough

This 10-minute tour follows one customer through the whole CRM. It is also a good demo script.
Everything you change updates the Dashboard and Reports immediately.

1. **Sign in and read the Dashboard.** Sign in with `mmitchell@hubspot.com` / `demo123`. The Dashboard
   shows the whole business: all companies and the whole team. Look at the chips under the title
   (overdue, due today, scheduled) and the six numbers across the top. Pick a company in the
   **All companies** selector to see just that account, then switch back.
2. **Find a customer.** Press `Ctrl K`, type **Lorelai**, press `Enter`. Her contact page opens with
   her details, company, deals, tickets and history.
3. **Open her company.** Click **The Dragonfly Inn**. The strip under the company name shows how
   everything connects: Company → Contacts → Deals → Activities → Tickets. Click any of those
   buttons to open that list.
4. **Look at the company's deals.** Open the **Deals** tab and click a deal. The deal panel slides in
   from the right with its value, stage bar, contact, close date and history.
5. **Move the deal through the pipeline.** Go to **Pipeline**. Drag a card from one column to the next
   (for example Contacted → Qualified). A message confirms the move and the numbers at the top
   update. Drag to **Won** to close it: its contact becomes a **Customer**.
6. **Log what happened.** Open the deal again → **Log activity**. Choose **Call**, enter a subject such
   as "Pricing discussion", and save. It appears on the deal, contact and company timelines.
7. **Plan the follow-up.** In the same panel click **Add task**. The title is pre-filled; set the due
   date to today and save.
8. **Complete the task.** Back on the Dashboard, the task is in **My Tasks**. Tick its circle. A
   "Task completed" message confirms it, and the due-today chip and sidebar number go down.
9. **Handle a support request.** Go to **Tickets**, open a ticket, add a note in **Activity** and press
   **Post**. Then click **Resolve ticket**. The open-ticket counts drop everywhere.
10. **Check the results.** Open **Reports** and choose **All time**. Won revenue, win rate, deals by
    stage and sales by owner all reflect what you just did.
11. **Ask the assistant.** Click **Ask AI** and try "What should the team focus on today?". The answer
    links straight to the deals, companies and tickets it mentions.

