## 5. Pages

### 5.1 Dashboard

**Where:** Sidebar → Dashboard (the first page after sign-in)

The overview of the whole business. It covers **all companies and the whole team**, not just the
signed-in person, and answers: what needs attention, how is the pipeline, and how are we doing?

| Section | What it shows | What you can do |
|---|---|---|
| Title and chips | "Business overview" (or the company's name when one is selected), with the team's overdue tasks, tasks due today and events scheduled today. | Click a chip to open Tasks or Calendar. |
| All companies selector | Which companies the page covers. | Pick one company to limit every card, chart and list to it. Choose **All companies** to go back. New deals and activities created from here are linked to the selected company. |
| Log activity · New deal | The two most common actions. | Opens the matching form. |
| Six number cards | **Total Contacts**, **New Leads** (leads added in the last 30 days), **Active Deals** (open deals), **Pipeline Value** (open deal amounts), **Won Revenue** (won in the last 30 days), **Open Tickets**. Each shows the change against the 30 days before, plus a small trend line. | Click a card to open its page. |
| Revenue Trend | Won revenue per month for the last 12 months, plus all-time won and this month. | Switch **Value** / **Deals** to see money or number of deals. Hover the line for exact figures. |
| Upcoming Tasks | The team's next open tasks, earliest first, with each assignee's initials. Overdue ones are red. | Tick to complete, click a title to edit, **Add task** to create one. |
| Sales Pipeline | Open deals per stage, as a coloured bar and as tiles with count and value. | Click a tile or **Open board** to go to the Pipeline. |
| Deal Conversion | Win rate ring, won vs lost count, average deal size, average sales cycle, weighted pipeline. | Read only. See section 8 for definitions. |
| Recent Deals | The latest deals with stage, amount and owner. | Click a row to open the deal panel. |
| Recent Activities | The latest completed calls, emails, meetings and notes. | Use the **…** menu to edit or delete. |
| Sales Performance | Team members ranked by won revenue, with won count and win rate. | Read only. |
| Top Customers | Companies with the most won revenue. | Click a company to open it. |

> **Note:** If a chart says "No deals closed-won with a close date in the last 12 months", your data
> simply has no recent wins. Reports → **All time** shows every closed deal.

### 5.2 Contacts

**Where:** Sidebar → Contacts

Every person you deal with. Each contact can belong to one company and can have deals, activities,
tasks, tickets and notes.

**The contacts list**

- **Tabs** across the top filter by status: All, Leads, Prospects, Customers, Inactives. The number
  shows how many are in each.
- **Search** by name, email, phone, company or job title.
- **All companies** filter shows only one company's contacts. **No company** lists contacts not linked to any company.
- **All owners** narrows to one team member's contacts.
- **Sort** by clicking a column heading. Click again to reverse, a third time to clear.
- **Columns** (top right of the table) shows or hides columns such as Phone, Owner, Last Activity,
  Created or Source.
- **Rows** at the bottom sets 10, 20 or 50 per page. Use the page numbers to move through the list.
- **Bulk actions**: tick rows on the left (the top box selects the whole page), then **Set status**,
  **Assign owner** or **Delete**.
- **Row menu** (**…** at the end of a row): Edit or Delete that contact.
- **Export** downloads the rows you see as a CSV file. **Add contact** opens the form.

**A contact's page** (click any row to open it)

| Area | What's there |
|---|---|
| Header | Name, status badge, job title and company. Quick buttons: **Call** and **Email** (open a pre-filled activity form; Email also tries to open your mail app), **Task**, **Note**, **Deal**. The **…** button has Edit and Delete. |
| About | Email, phone, company, owner, lead source, created date, and any extra fields that came from your CSV files (for example Favorite food or Company roles). **Edit** changes them. |
| Company card | The contact's company. Click to open it. |
| Four figures | Open pipeline, Won revenue, Open tasks, Last contacted. |
| Tabs | **Timeline** (everything that happened, newest first), **Deals**, **Activities**, **Tasks**, **Notes** (write a note at the top, `Ctrl Enter` to save). |

### 5.3 Companies

**Where:** Sidebar → Companies

The organisations you sell to or support. A company pulls together all its contacts, deals,
activities and tickets.

**The companies list**

- Shows each company's location, number of contacts, open pipeline and won revenue. It starts sorted
  by won revenue, highest first.
- Search by name, city, industry or website. Filter by industry or owner. **Columns** adds Industry,
  Open Tickets, Size or Created.
- Tick rows to **Delete** several at once. **Export** and **Add company** are at the top.

**A company's page**

- **Quick buttons**: Contact, Deal, Activity, Ticket, Note. Anything you create here is linked to the
  company automatically.
- **Relationship strip**: Company → Contacts → Deals → Activities → Tickets, with counts. Click any
  step to open that tab.
- **About**: industry, size, phone, location, account owner, date added and extra CSV fields (such as
  "Also known as" or "Associated companies").
- **Figures**: open pipeline, won revenue, open tickets, last activity.
- **Tabs**: Timeline, Contacts, Deals, Activities, Tickets, Notes.

### 5.4 Deals and the deal panel

**Where:** Sidebar → Deals

A deal is a sales opportunity with an amount, a stage and an expected close date. The Deals page is
the list view; the Pipeline is the board view of the same deals.

**The deals list**

- **Tabs**: Open (default), Won, Lost, All deals.
- **Summary tiles** above the table: total value, weighted value (Open tab) or average deal size,
  number of deals, high-priority count. They follow your filters.
- **Filters**: search by deal or company, stage, priority, owner.
- Sorted by **Expected Close**, soonest first. Open deals past their close date are marked red with "overdue".
- **Bulk actions**: tick rows → **Move to stage** or **Delete**.
- **Board view** switches to the Pipeline. **Export** and **New deal** are at the top.

**The deal panel**

Clicking a deal anywhere in the app (list, board, dashboard, search, contact or company page) opens
this panel on the right. Press `Esc` or the **×** to close it.

| Part | What it does |
|---|---|
| Top icons | Edit (pencil), Delete (bin), Close (×). |
| Stage bar | Shows how far the deal has progressed. **Click any stage** to move the deal there. |
| Mark won / Mark lost | Closes the deal. Winning also turns its contact into a Customer. Closed deals show **Reopen deal** instead. |
| Details | Contact, company, expected close, probability and weighted value, priority, owner, plus imported fields such as HubSpot stage, Pipeline, Product of interest, Currency or Line items. |
| Log activity · Add task | Creates a record already linked to this deal, its contact and its company. |
| Timeline · Tasks | The deal's history (stage changes, activities, notes) and its tasks, which you can tick off here. |

### 5.5 Pipeline

**Where:** Sidebar → Pipeline (or **Board view** on Deals)

A board with one column per stage. Each card is a deal. Moving cards is the fastest way to keep the
pipeline current.

- **Figures at the top**: Total pipeline, Weighted pipeline, Open deals, Won value, Win rate. They
  update the moment you move a card.
- **Filter** by deal or company name, or by owner. Untick **Show won / lost** to hide the closed columns.
- **Each column** shows its deal count and total value. The **+** in the header or **Add deal** at
  the bottom creates a deal already in that stage.
- **Each card** shows deal name, company, amount, priority, expected close date (amber if within
  7 days, red if past) and the owner's initials.
- **Drag a card** to another column to change its stage. The column you're over is highlighted, and a
  message confirms the move.
- **Click a card** to open the deal panel. The card's **…** menu has Open, Edit, Mark won, Mark lost and Delete.

> **Phones:** Dragging works with a mouse or trackpad. On a phone or tablet, tap the card and use the
> stage bar in the deal panel instead.

### 5.6 Activities

**Where:** Sidebar → Activities

A log of every interaction: Call, Email, Meeting, Note, Follow-up. Activities are either **Planned**
(in the future) or **Completed**.

- **Tabs** filter by type. Search by subject, description, contact or company. **Everyone** narrows to
  one person. **All / Planned / Completed** filters by status.
- **Upcoming** lists planned activities, soonest first. Click **Done** when one has happened.
- **History** lists completed activities grouped by day. **Load more** shows older ones.
- **Today's Schedule** (right) lists today's activities by time. Its **+** schedules a new one.
- **Last 7 Days** (right) counts completed activities by type.
- Each activity's **…** menu has Edit and Delete. **Log activity** is at the top.

### 5.7 Tasks

**Where:** Sidebar → Tasks

Your to-do list. A task has a due date, a priority and an assignee, and can be linked to a contact,
company or deal.

- **My tasks / All tasks** at the top right switches between your own tasks and the whole team's.
- **Four cards**: Overdue, Due today, Upcoming, Done this week. Click a card to filter to it.
- **Tabs**: All (grouped into Overdue, Today, Upcoming, Completed), Today, Upcoming, Overdue, Completed.
- **Filters**: search, priority, and assignee (under All tasks).
- **Complete** a task by clicking its round checkbox. Click again to reopen it. Click the title to
  edit, or use **…** to edit or delete.
- Under each title: the due date (red "Overdue", amber "Today") and the deal or company it relates to.

### 5.8 Calendar

**Where:** Sidebar → Calendar

A month view of activities and task due dates.

- **My calendar / Team** switches between your items and everyone's.
- Move between months with **‹** and **›**. **Today** jumps back to the current month. Today's date is circled.
- Each day shows up to three items, coloured by activity type. Tasks start with ✓. Faded items are done.
- **Click a day** to list everything on it in the right-hand panel. From there, **+ Task** adds a task
  due that day and **+ Event** schedules an activity at 10:00 that day.
- **Schedule** at the top creates a planned meeting on the selected day.

### 5.9 Tickets

**Where:** Sidebar → Tickets

Customer support requests. Every ticket has a number (for example #1010), a priority, a status and
an assignee, and can be linked to a contact and company.

**The tickets list**

- **Four cards**: Open tickets, Urgent / High, Avg resolution time, Resolved in the last 7 days.
- **Tabs**: Active (Open + In Progress + Waiting, the default), then each status, then All.
- **Filters**: search by subject, number or company; priority; assignee.
- **Bulk actions**: tick rows → **Set status**, **Assign** or **Delete**.

**A ticket's page**

- **Resolve ticket** (or **Reopen** once closed), Edit, Delete.
- **Status bar**: Open → In Progress → Waiting → Resolved → Closed. Click a step to set it.
- **Activity**: write an internal note or record your reply and press **Post**. Status changes are
  logged here automatically.
- **Details**: change Status, Priority or Assignee from the dropdowns (saved immediately). Also shows
  created, updated and resolved times, and imported fields such as Source or Issue of interest.
- **Customer**: the linked contact, their email, company and account owner.

### 5.10 Reports

**Where:** Sidebar → Reports

Analytics for managers and anyone preparing a review. Choose the period at the top right:
**All time** (default), **30 days**, **90 days** or **12 months**. With a period other than All time,
each figure is compared with the period just before it.

| Report | Answers |
|---|---|
| Six figures | Won revenue, deals won, win rate, average deal size, conversion rate, average sales cycle. |
| Revenue by Month | How much was won in each of the last 12 months. |
| Deals by Stage | How many deals are in each stage and their value. |
| Sales by Owner | Who won the most, with win rate and open deals. |
| Activity Performance | How many calls, emails, meetings, notes and follow-ups each person completed. |
| Customer Growth | How the number of contacts has grown over the year. |
| Lead Sources | Where contacts come from and what share became customers. |

**Export** downloads the figures, the per-person table and the monthly numbers as one CSV file.

### 5.11 Settings

**Where:** Sidebar → Settings (or the profile menu)

- **Profile & workspace**: change your name, email and the workspace name, then **Save changes**.
- **Preferences**: Appearance (Light / Dark) and Currency (US Dollar / Indian Rupee). Currency changes
  the symbol and number format only; amounts are not converted.
- **Team**: everyone in the workspace with their role.
- **Data**: record counts, **Re-import CSV data** and **Clear all data**. See section 7.
- **Data sources**: one row per CSV file, showing how many rows it had, what new records it created,
